From: Frida Hou <Frida-a@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 01:52:22 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [QW38] GDN in_proj_ba: bit-exact sequential-K Triton GEMM for
 M=2..4 on SM120

cuBLAS picks cutlass_80_wmma 16x16 (8 single-warp CTAs, ~34 us cold, ~52 us in
serving) for in_proj_ba (N=96, K=5120) at M=2..4, i.e. MTP k=3 decode at one
request. The Triton kernel runs the same sequential k16 HMMA chain (no split-K),
bit-identical to that kernel on SM120, at ~9 us. Other M and other archs keep
cuBLAS. VLLM_GDN_BA_SEQK=0 disables it; one-time proof log line.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
